{"availability":"available","full":"LPC4/Full-Stack","name":"Full-Stack","description":"A compiler, assembler, and RISC-V VM, and kernel implementation, all running in real time in your browser.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":88,"forks":8,"created":"2026-04-13T17:28:30Z","updated":"2026-08-20T11:34:42Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lpc4.github.io/Full-Stack/","topics":["assembler","compiler","riscv64","virtual-machine","wasm"],"demo":"https://lpc4.github.io/Full-Stack/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.728Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.728Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.728Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.728Z","stars":88,"forks":8}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Full-Stack is a self-contained compiler pipeline for a small systems language (HLL). It carries source all the way to machine code and runs the result on a built-in RISC-V CPU, with every stage inspectable in a graphical IDE:","The whole toolchain is written in Rust and runs either natively (egui desktop IDE and a fsc CLI) or fully client-side in the browser via WebAssembly, VM included. The kernel target boots a real S-mode operating system on the VM: paging, processes, a filesystem, an interactive shell, a line editor, and a compiler toolchain that runs inside the VM so you can write, compile, assemble, and run a program without ever leaving the machine.","Boot the kernel target (the IDE's machine dock, or fsc run kernel.elf) and you land at a shell prompt running as pid 1:"],"features":["A self-hosting toolchain inside the VM. Boot the kernel, drop into the shell, write","an .hll or .s file in the in-VM editor, compile it with cc, assemble it with as, link it with ld, and run the result, all without leaving the guest. The compiler (/bin/cc), assembler (/bin/as), and linker (/bin/ld) are…","A real interactive OS. An S-mode kernel with Sv39 paging, per-process address","spaces, a round-robin preemptive scheduler, an inode read-write filesystem, and a shell with pipes, redirection, background jobs, and file management. Foreground programs return to the prompt on exit and can be…","A complete front-to-back compiler. Lexer, parser, semantic analysis, typed SSA"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LPC4/Full-Stack/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7956ee860f55c5194fe1fbd8d827cb75912fe916683d8b68c79be7e3e04e4d08","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.940Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.940Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Full-Stack is a self-contained compiler pipeline for a small systems language (HLL). It carries source all the way to machine code and runs the result on a built-in RISC-V CPU, with every stage inspectable in a graphical IDE:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LPC4/Full-Stack/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7956ee860f55c5194fe1fbd8d827cb75912fe916683d8b68c79be7e3e04e4d08","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LPC4/Full-Stack/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.940Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-20T11:34:42Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LPC4/Full-Stack/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:29.941Z","hash":"7956ee860f55c5194fe1fbd8d827cb75912fe916683d8b68c79be7e3e04e4d08","originalBytes":12134,"storedBytes":12134,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["run","fsc","hll","kernel","assembly","crates","programs","build","cargo","compile","compiler","shell","ide","machine","bin","editor","framebuffer","release","risc-v","source","specifications.md","boot","elf","language","live","pipeline","test","uart","assemble","assembler","filesystem","linker","object","real","runs","stage","tests","through","user","analysis","built","cpu","each","full","full-stack","hll-to-ir","hosted","keyboard","link","parser","plus","program","program.hll","small","specification.md","su